1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,259
One masked line. It plots one subgroup of film thickness

2
00:00:04,359 --> 00:00:09,164
every sampling interval, and nothing else about it matters yet.

3
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:12,546
This is the same process Act A was looking

4
00:00:12,646 --> 00:00:15,942
at, drawn above the line it is running on.

5
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:20,162
Somewhere along this run the mean really moves, and then

6
00:00:20,262 --> 00:00:24,165
it stays moved. Watch how little the picture changes.

7
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:28,085
The line is sampled on a clock. One step along the

8
00:00:28,185 --> 00:00:32,886
strip is one interval, and every interval is the same length.

9
00:00:32,983 --> 00:00:37,570
Sometimes the chart alarms and nothing has changed. The line

10
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:41,163
stops for one check, and that is charged once.

11
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:45,518
Once. It does not keep costing anything after the check.

12
00:00:47,016 --> 00:00:51,516
And while nobody has noticed, every subgroup after the move is

13
00:00:51,616 --> 00:00:56,190
produced against a mean that is already wrong. That is reworked

14
00:00:56,290 --> 00:00:59,900
at the next step, and it is charged by the minute.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,612
Nobody has to be told which of those two is the

16
00:01:03,712 --> 00:01:08,588
expensive one. One block stopped. The other one is still going.

17
00:01:08,683 --> 00:01:12,195
Four facts about one line. Everything after

18
00:01:12,295 --> 00:01:14,967
this is arithmetic on those four.

19
00:01:16,266 --> 00:01:20,297
Three rule sets are on offer for this line. Not every

20
00:01:20,397 --> 00:01:24,974
combination — these three, in the order the page lists them.

21
00:01:25,066 --> 00:01:30,143
Each one buys its alarms at a rate that never changes. That rate is

22
00:01:30,243 --> 00:01:34,470
the price. What it buys is what we are about to look at.

23
00:01:34,566 --> 00:01:39,314
One point beyond three sigma, and nothing else. It waits.

24
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:43,956
Add the two-of-three rule and the same run is flagged sooner.

25
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:47,694
All four, and the same run is flagged sooner again —

26
00:01:47,794 --> 00:01:52,374
and flagged back there, in the stretch where nothing had changed.

27
00:01:52,466 --> 00:01:56,310
So the plate that alarms earliest is the same plate that

28
00:01:56,410 --> 00:02:00,816
alarms when nothing happened. Both halves of the purchase are on

29
00:02:00,916 --> 00:02:04,126
the strip, and neither of them has a price yet.

30
00:02:04,216 --> 00:02:08,628
Pick one now. The prices are off screen on purpose.

31
00:02:09,216 --> 00:02:12,595
Now the prices, and every one of them is carried

32
00:02:12,695 --> 00:02:16,364
out of that strip rather than typed onto the screen.

33
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:20,837
One point beyond three sigma waits the longest, so its stack

34
00:02:20,937 --> 00:02:24,726
of wasted minutes is the tallest thing on the board.

35
00:02:24,816 --> 00:02:27,736
Two rules cut the waiting by more than

36
00:02:27,836 --> 00:02:30,596
half, and buy fewer alarms doing it.

37
00:02:30,683 --> 00:02:33,975
All four cut the waiting again, and this time

38
00:02:34,075 --> 00:02:36,991
the alarm half goes up rather than down.

39
00:02:37,083 --> 00:02:41,100
Three prices, one case. And the plate that bought the

40
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:44,519
fewest false alarms is not the one that won.

41
00:02:44,616 --> 00:02:48,234
Same four facts, three prices. One is smaller,

42
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:51,548
and that is arithmetic rather than taste.

43
00:02:51,633 --> 00:02:55,082
Two terms, in the colours of the two stacks they

44
00:02:55,182 --> 00:02:58,853
were built from. Nothing else is in the arithmetic.

45
00:02:58,950 --> 00:03:04,082
The cheapest one on this line, priced from this line's own four facts.

46
00:03:04,166 --> 00:03:08,770
Three of those four facts are about to be held completely still.

47
00:03:08,866 --> 00:03:12,482
One row is still lit. Before I touch it: decide

48
00:03:12,582 --> 00:03:16,830
whether moving it can change which rule set is correct.

49
00:03:17,416 --> 00:03:21,533
The line now expects a 3 sigma move rather than

50
00:03:21,633 --> 00:03:24,852
a 1 sigma one. That is the only edit.

51
00:03:24,950 --> 00:03:28,920
Every rule set now sees it in about two subgroups, so

52
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:32,914
the waiting collapses for all three of them at once.

53
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,851
The rates the plates buy their alarms at did not move

54
00:03:36,951 --> 00:03:40,580
at all. The purchase price is exactly what it was.

55
00:03:40,666 --> 00:03:43,981
At this scale all three are nearly nothing,

56
00:03:44,081 --> 00:03:46,998
so the board rescales to what is left.

57
00:03:47,083 --> 00:03:49,958
I changed one line of the case. The

58
00:03:50,058 --> 00:03:53,103
rules did not change. The answer did.

59
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:57,641
The extra rules still cost what they always cost. Against a

60
00:03:57,741 --> 00:04:01,644
move this size they simply have nothing left to buy.

61
00:04:01,733 --> 00:04:06,289
Put the arithmetic away. It has already done its job.

62
00:04:06,383 --> 00:04:09,340
What is left is the line, back at full

63
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:13,603
width, running the rule set this case actually chose.

64
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:18,136
Every subgroup it plotted, in the order it plotted them.

65
00:04:18,233 --> 00:04:20,197
It alarms here.

66
00:04:20,283 --> 00:04:23,214
Everything from that subgroup on is held

67
00:04:23,314 --> 00:04:25,943
at the next step instead of shipped.

68
00:04:26,033 --> 00:04:29,079
Everything between the move and the alarm

69
00:04:29,179 --> 00:04:31,765
is pulled back and looked at again.

70
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:34,903
And the reason is written down against the

71
00:04:35,003 --> 00:04:37,606
size of move it was bought to catch.

72
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:41,017
You are not choosing a rule set. You are choosing

73
00:04:41,117 --> 00:04:44,296
what the next shift does when the chart alarms.

